WEBVTT

00:00:00.411 --> 00:00:07.940
In this video, you will sign up for the weekly lights email, one short email a week with the lights and events near a city you choose.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.837
It is free, and you can stop it any time.

00:00:10.837 --> 00:00:11.815
We start on the map.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.539
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:17.239 --> 00:00:19.789
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:21.429 --> 00:00:22.409
Then tap Allow.

00:00:25.778 --> 00:00:28.884
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:28.884 --> 00:00:30.261
See the three dots?

00:00:30.261 --> 00:00:34.430
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:35.109
Tap them.

00:00:37.663 --> 00:00:40.019
In the menu, tap Weekly lights email.

00:00:41.631 --> 00:00:44.223
Type your email address, then your city.

00:00:44.223 --> 00:00:47.546
We use the city to choose which lights and events to send you.

00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:53.060
You can also choose how far from the city to look: five, ten, or twenty five miles.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.755
Then tick the box to agree to get the email.

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:58.712
It is a free email, once a week, and nothing else.

00:01:00.258 --> 00:01:01.217
Tap Sign up.

00:01:03.224 --> 00:01:05.429
We send you an email to confirm.

00:01:05.429 --> 00:01:10.711
Nothing is sent until you do, and that protects you from anyone signing you up by mistake.

00:01:10.711 --> 00:01:12.381
Open it, and tap the link.

00:01:14.331 --> 00:01:15.061
That is it.

00:01:15.061 --> 00:01:18.619
You will get one email a week with the lights and events near you.

00:01:18.619 --> 00:01:21.469
And every email ends with a link to stop.

00:01:21.469 --> 00:01:24.928
One tap, and you are off the list, no questions asked.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:28.872
Next up: Install the app and use it offline.
